"use strict";(self.webpackChunk_N_E=self.webpackChunk_N_E||[]).push([[7401],{67401:e=>{e.exports=JSON.parse('{"slug":"vvp-kitaya-3-kvartal-2026-eksport","locale":"en","title":"China\'s economy accelerates to 4.5% on exports while retail sales grow only 1.1%","description":"China\'s GDP grew 4.5% in quarter III of 2026. Exports rose 36%, retail sales 1.1%. Why externally driven growth is fragile and what it means for Russia.","blocks":[{"id":"b001","kind":"paragraph","text":"China\'s GDP grew by 4.5% in July–September compared with the same period of 2025, according to data published on October 19. Analysts expected 4.4%. Quarter II growth was 4.3%, the weakest since 2022. The economy expanded by 1.2% from the previous quarter. Growth over 9 months was 4.6%, with GDP totaling 107.1 trillion yuan. The government\'s annual target is 4.5–5%, which looks achievable after these figures."},{"id":"b002","kind":"paragraph","text":"Exports provided the main contribution. In September they grew by 36.3% year-on-year, while imports rose by 31%. China sold $133.5 billion more goods abroad than it purchased over the month, the largest gap in 20 months. Chip exports doubled in value over 9 months; computers and cars increased by about 54%. Industrial production rose by 5.5% in September."},{"id":"b003","kind":"paragraph","text":"The domestic picture is different. September retail sales grew by 1.1%, better than the expected 0.5% but still weak. Fixed-asset investment over 9 months fell by 7.2%, private investment by 10.4%, and housing-construction investment by 20.6%. New-apartment sales by floor area declined by 13.2%. Much of Chinese households\' savings is invested in apartments; when homes become cheaper, people feel poorer and spend more cautiously."},{"id":"b004","kind":"paragraph","text":"Imagine a family cafe starting to deliver pies to a neighboring town. Revenue rises and cooks are busy, but local residents visit less often. While the neighbors keep buying, the cafe does well. If they find another bakery, growth ends because the cafe has not expanded its own customer base. Economists call this growth driven by external demand. It is fast but depends on others\' decisions: the European Union is already pressing China to sell it fewer high-value goods."},{"id":"b005","kind":"paragraph","text":"For Russia, export revenue is at stake. China is the largest buyer of Russian fuel: in September it purchased about 9.1 billion euros of oil, gas and coal. Busy factories consume more energy, so raw-material demand holds up while export orders continue. Strong data reduce the likelihood of new domestic-demand support: when the target is being met, Beijing has less reason to spend on stimulus."},{"id":"b006","kind":"paragraph","text":"Economist Intelligence Unit senior economist Tianchen Xu expects exports and state investment to support growth in quarter IV as well. The risk is reliance on one pillar. Slower global AI investment or European Union barriers would hurt chip and machinery sales, while domestic buyers are not yet ready to replace foreign ones. Sustained export demand keeps Chinese factories busy and Russian-oil purchases supported. Weaker external demand would test how quickly Beijing can stimulate domestic consumption."},{"id":"b007","kind":"heading","text":"How much did China\'s GDP grow in quarter III of 2026?"},{"id":"b008","kind":"paragraph","text":"By 4.5% compared with July–September 2025. Analysts expected 4.4%; quarter II growth was 4.3%, the weakest since 2022. The economy grew by 4.6% over 9 months against the government\'s 4.5–5% target."},{"id":"b009","kind":"heading","text":"Why is China\'s growth described as unbalanced?"},{"id":"b010","kind":"paragraph","text":"September exports rose by 36.3%, but retail sales by only 1.1%. Property investment fell by 20.6% over 9 months. Growth is driven by foreign buyers rather than domestic residents."},{"id":"b011","kind":"heading","text":"What does faster Chinese growth mean for Russia?"},{"id":"b012","kind":"paragraph","text":"China is the largest buyer of Russian oil, gas and coal. Fuel demand holds up while its factories are busy with export orders. If external demand weakens, China\'s domestic market is not yet ready to replace it."}],"sources":[{"label":"China\'s GDP grows 4.5% in quarter III","url":"https://www.interfax.ru/business/1123374"},{"label":"China\'s economic growth quickens as exports surge","url":"https://www.cnbc.com/2026/10/19/chinas-economic-growth-quickens-to-4point6percent-as-exports-surge-stimulus-rolls-out.html"},{"label":"China\'s Growth Rebounds to 4.5%, Puts Annual Target Within Reach","url":"https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2026-10-19/china-s-growth-rebounds-to-4-5-puts-annual-target-within-reach"},{"label":"China Q3 GDP beats forecasts at 4.5%, retail sales grow at fastest pace since March","url":"https://investinglive.com/news/china-q3-gdp-beats-forecasts-at-4-5-retail-sales-grow-at-fastest-pace-since-march/"},{"label":"China\'s economy holds steady in first three quarters of 2026","url":"https://www.indexbox.io/blog/chinas-economy-holds-steady-in-first-three-quarters-of-2026-as-trade-and-industry-outpace-broader-growth/"},{"label":"China\'s exports surge 36.3% in September as pressure ramps up to rebalance trade","url":"https://clickondetroit.com/business/2026/10/14/chinas-exports-surge-363-in-september-as-pressure-ramps-up-to-rebalance-trade"},{"label":"China Posts Biggest Trade Surplus in 20 Months","url":"https://tradingeconomics.com/china/balance-of-trade/news/591695"},{"label":"September 2026 — Monthly analysis of Russian fossil fuel exports and sanctions","url":"https://energyandcleanair.org/september-2026-monthly-analysis-of-russian-fossil-fuel-exports-and-sanctions/"}],"sourceBodySha256":"a43116f5bc45095d81495bfb1beae8eb81d22f98eafffb5342e2297d883572c6"}')}}]);